\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Corollary}
\title{Inserting a unit of flux}
\date{2026-11-27}

\p{Suppose two neighboring scalar fluxes #{w,w+1} are realized in the angle window of \ref{fdip-019X}, with the same graded spin module and mass. The difference of their indices, in that order from #{w} to #{w+1}, is #{-s\kappa(M)}. Their constant-curvature representatives can be joined by a scalar link path.}

\proof{\p{Subtract the two index formulas. To construct the path write #{V=N_1N_2}, select a plaquette #{p_0}, and start at the uniform angle #{2\pi w/V}. Add to each lifted real angle the increment #{2\pi t(V^{-1}-\mathbf{1}_{p=p_0})}. These increments sum to zero, so the edge-cochain construction of \ref{fdip-01A4} realizes them on links. At #{t=1} their phases all equal #{\ue^{2\pi\ui(w+1)/V}}. The flat adjustment in that lemma fixes any prescribed endpoint holonomies. An intermediate field can leave the angle window. Varying one plaquette alone with the others fixed would violate the unit product on the torus.}}
